# Copy to .env.local and fill in. Never commit .env.local.
# No key here may ever be prefixed NEXT_PUBLIC_ — see ARCHITECTURE.md §7.

# Public site URL, used for metadata, sitemap and canonical URLs
NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=http://localhost:3000

# --- Phase 10: Ask the Lab ---
# Provider: Groq (console.groq.com — free tier, no card required, no new
# SDK dependency, called via plain fetch()). Without these two set, the
# assistant serves the honest "AI CORE TEMPORARILY OFFLINE" state — see
# AI_SPEC.md §7. Never prefix either with NEXT_PUBLIC_.
# AI_PROVIDER_API_KEY=
# AI_MODEL=openai/gpt-oss-20b
# A reasoning model — Groq requires reasoning_effort:"low" for it (already
# set in lib/ai/groq-client.ts whenever AI_MODEL starts with "openai/gpt-oss")
# or its hidden "thinking" tokens can consume the whole max_tokens budget
# against a system prompt this long, coming back with an empty answer.
# Confirmed against the live API on 2026-09-05 — llama-3.3-70b-versatile,
# the model this was originally scoped against, has since been removed
# from Groq's lineup; re-check `GET /openai/v1/models` before changing this.
# Bumped from 200 (2026-09-05): openai/gpt-oss-20b's hidden reasoning tokens
# share this budget, and the knowledge corpus has grown enough (experience +
# 2 new projects) that 200 started coming back empty on some questions.
# Re-check if the corpus grows substantially again.
# AI_MAX_OUTPUT_TOKENS=500
# AI_TEMPERATURE=0.3
# Failover chain, tried in order after AI_MODEL. Groq enforces its
# tokens-per-minute limit PER MODEL on separate budgets (verified via
# x-ratelimit-limit-tokens, 2026-09-18: 8,000 TPM each for gpt-oss-20b,
# gpt-oss-120b and qwen3.8-27b), so listing more models multiplies how many
# visitors can be served per minute. It does NOT raise the ceiling on a
# single request — one question is answered by one model. Comma-separated.
# AI_MODEL_FALLBACKS=qwen/qwen3.8-27b,openai/gpt-oss-120b

# The per-minute token allowance of ONE model on your Groq plan. Used only
# to derive the grounding corpus's size budget in lib/ai/knowledge.ts, which
# e2e/knowledge-budget.spec.ts asserts in `npm run verify`. Raise it when you
# upgrade the Groq plan — never to silence a failing build.
# AI_TOKENS_PER_MINUTE=8000

# Prompt-injection classifier (meta-llama/llama-prompt-guard-2-86m), layered
# on top of the regex patterns in lib/ai/guardrails.ts. Its own rate-limit
# pool, so it costs no answering capacity. Set to "false" to disable.
# AI_PROMPT_GUARD_ENABLED=true
# AI_INJECTION_THRESHOLD=0.5

# Spoken answers. OFF until set. canopylabs/orpheus-v1-english requires the
# Groq ORG ADMIN to accept the model's terms first — until then every call
# returns model_terms_required and the "Listen" button stays hidden:
#   https://console.groq.com/playground?model=canopylabs%2Forpheus-v1-english
# Accept the terms, set this, and the button appears with no code change.
# AI_TTS_MODEL=canopylabs/orpheus-v1-english
# AI_TTS_VOICE=tara

# AI_RATE_LIMIT_PER_IP_PER_HOUR=10
# AI_RATE_LIMIT_GLOBAL_PER_DAY=200
# AI_MONTHLY_SPEND_CAP_USD=10
# AI_PRICE_PER_1K_TOKENS_USD=0.001

# Base URL scripts/generate-canned-answers.mjs POSTs to — a running
# `npm run dev` or `npm start` locally, or the deployed site.
# ASK_LAB_BASE_URL=http://localhost:3000
